    "published": "2026-08-17T11:16:41.427",
    "vulnStatus": "Analyzed",
    "descriptions": [
     {
      "lang": "en",
      "value": "openssl_encrypt versions before 1.4.6 contain a key derivation flaw in sequential XOR composition mode where the last stage cancels out during key generation. When configured with a single KDF and no prior hashing stage, attackers can bypass memory-hard key derivation and perform offline password cracking at SHA-256 speed instead of the configured KDF cost."
     }
